# FIX-P12-4 — POST auto-ID + search-based _meta read + withRetry throw fix
# Executed: 2026-07-18
# Status: CLOSED

## Root Cause (F-4)
AOSS VECTORSEARCH collections reject client-supplied document IDs.
bulk-index.ts used PUT /_doc/chunk-N; meta-doc.ts used PUT/GET /_doc/_cumplify_iso_kb_meta.
All returned HTTP 400: "Document ID is not supported in create/index operation request".
Constraint documented in-repo (aoss-prover.ts) — shared blind spot.

## Fix
1. bulk-index.ts: `PUT /{index}/_doc/chunk-{i}` → `POST /{index}/_doc` (auto-ID)
   - Mirrors aoss-prover.ts proven pattern

2. meta-doc.ts:
   - Write: `PUT /{index}/_doc/{id}` → `POST /{index}/_doc` (auto-ID)
   - Read: `GET /{index}/_doc/{id}` → `POST /{index}/_search` with query:
     `{bool:{filter:[{term:{'metadata.tenantId':'__META__'}},{term:{'metadata.clauseRef':'_meta'}}]}},size:1`
     → `hits.hits[0]._source.contentHash ?? null`
   - Old _meta doc dies with index deletion on re-seed (no duplicate concern)

3. aoss-retry.ts:
   - withRetry throw message reports actual `attempts` count (was hardcoded MAX_ATTEMPTS)
   - aossReadOp signature accepts optional body (needed for POST _search)

4. handler.unit.test.ts: mocks updated for POST _search pattern + method-aware
   responses (DELETE→200, PUT→200, POST→201)

5. aoss-retry.test.ts: non-retryable assertion checks "FAILED after 1 attempts"

## Evidence
